# BeebAsm Extensions Summary

This document summarizes the custom extensions added to BeebAsm by LoveBug.

---

## 1. MULTIPASS

BeebAsm now uses an iterative multi-pass approach instead of strict 2-pass assembly.

### Problem with 2-Pass
- Pass 1 calculates label addresses assuming forward references are 3-byte (Absolute)
- Pass 2 might discover a Zero Page reference and optimize to 2-byte
- This changes all subsequent addresses → "Inconsistent Code" crash

### Multi-Pass Solution
- Pass 1: Discovery (same as before)
- Pass 2+: Refinement - if code shrinks, update and continue
- Repeats until `g_CodeChanged == false` (stabilizes)
- Final pass generates output

### Safety
- Max 10 passes prevents infinite loops
- Code only shrinks (monotonic), guaranteeing convergence

