## 2. XORG Directive

Extended ORG for interleaved assembly across multiple memory areas.

### Syntax
```
XORG <expression>    ; Static origin
XORG <symbol>        ; Tracking origin (symbol linked to P%)
```

### Static Origin
```
XORG &2000           ; Same as ORG &2000
```

### Tracking Origin
```
main = &1000
swr  = &8000

mainPc = main        ; Cursor for main RAM
xorg mainPc          ; P% = mainPc, link mainPc to P%

... assemble code ...

swrPc = swr          ; Cursor for sideways RAM
xorg swrPc           ; P% = swrPc, link swrPc to P%

... assemble code ...

xorg mainPc          ; Resume where we left off in main ram
```

### Behavior
- Links a symbol to the Program Counter (P%)
- As code is assembled, the linked symbol auto-updates
- Unlinks previous symbol when switching to new XORG or using ORG

